# private-files/ is committed on purpose -- that folder IS how a file gets to
# Jesse. It is kept off the web by the 404 rule in netlify.toml, not by being
# absent from the repo. Remember the repo is public: nothing secret goes in it.

# SS-602 identifier denylist. The terms are employer, client, facility and
# person names that must never appear on the site -- so committing them to a
# PUBLIC repository would publish the exact strings the rule exists to catch.
# data/denylist.example.json is the committed, redacted template.
.denylist.local.json
